WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.143 --> 00:00:02.210
- [Voiceover] Gluten-free
diets that cut out all food

00:00:02.210 --> 00:00:04.717
with wheat, barley, and rye have become

00:00:04.717 --> 00:00:07.713
extremely popular in
the last couple years,

00:00:07.713 --> 00:00:10.220
so we challenged four
people to change their diet

00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:12.612
for a month to see what happens

00:00:12.612 --> 00:00:14.376
when you go gluten-free.

00:00:14.376 --> 00:00:15.445
- I've heard that going gluten-free

00:00:15.445 --> 00:00:16.856
helps you get more energetic

00:00:16.856 --> 00:00:18.431
which is definitely
something I'm interested in

00:00:18.431 --> 00:00:20.097
because I'm always tired.

00:00:20.097 --> 00:00:21.498
- I wanna kinda get back onto

00:00:21.498 --> 00:00:23.576
a healthy eating schedule

00:00:23.576 --> 00:00:24.999
and really pay more attention

00:00:24.999 --> 00:00:25.943
to what I'm putting in my body.

00:00:25.943 --> 00:00:30.424
- I'm excited to just find
good gluten-free cake.

00:00:30.424 --> 00:00:31.697
- The reason I wanna go gluten-free

00:00:31.697 --> 00:00:33.693
is because my girlfriend was diagnosed

00:00:33.693 --> 00:00:35.017
with celiac disease

00:00:37.557 --> 00:00:39.605
and I'm hoping that by myself

00:00:39.605 --> 00:00:40.878
going gluten-free, I can make it

00:00:40.878 --> 00:00:42.237
a little bit easier for her.

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:45.187
- What are some changes
that I should expect

00:00:45.187 --> 00:00:46.742
when going gluten-free?

00:00:46.742 --> 00:00:48.228
- It depends on how sensitive your body

00:00:48.228 --> 00:00:50.411
is to gluten, but some
of the great benefits

00:00:50.411 --> 00:00:52.895
of being gluten-free are increased energy.

00:00:52.895 --> 00:00:55.031
A lot of people who go
on a gluten-free diet

00:00:55.031 --> 00:00:57.139
end up having more energy just because

00:00:57.139 --> 00:00:59.486
the energy in their body isn't
being used for digestion.

00:00:59.486 --> 00:01:01.390
- I'm nervous that I'm not
gonna have a lot to eat.

00:01:01.390 --> 00:01:02.527
- Think about it this way:

00:01:02.527 --> 00:01:04.269
our favorite foods
become our favorite foods

00:01:04.269 --> 00:01:05.801
because we eat them often.

00:01:05.801 --> 00:01:07.171
The good news for you is you're not

00:01:07.171 --> 00:01:08.588
giving up your five favorite.

00:01:08.588 --> 00:01:10.538
You're just setting it aside and saying,

00:01:10.538 --> 00:01:12.001
"Oh, do I have 20 other favorites

00:01:12.001 --> 00:01:13.273
"that I didn't even know about?"

00:01:13.273 --> 00:01:15.038
- That's exciting (laughs).
- So you come out of the diet

00:01:15.038 --> 00:01:17.035
and you've got 25 favorites.

00:01:19.835 --> 00:01:22.296
- I was just looking at
my favorite fake bacon

00:01:22.296 --> 00:01:23.921
that I eat all the time.

00:01:23.921 --> 00:01:27.075
Modern corn starch, wheat, gluten!

00:01:27.075 --> 00:01:29.188
I had no idea there was gluten in this.

00:01:29.188 --> 00:01:31.453
I might've eaten some
since I started the diet.

00:01:32.735 --> 00:01:33.687
I definitely have.

00:01:33.687 --> 00:01:35.429
- At work, we had free cupcake day,

00:01:35.429 --> 00:01:38.076
so I after I pouted about
that quietly to myself,

00:01:38.076 --> 00:01:40.351
I suddenly found out there
was a gluten-free option.

00:01:40.351 --> 00:01:42.232
There's gluten-free
options of a lot of stuff,

00:01:42.232 --> 00:01:44.716
but there's just one gluten-free option.

00:01:44.716 --> 00:01:46.063
- I've found it's made my life

00:01:46.063 --> 00:01:48.849
about 60% more annoying.

00:01:48.849 --> 00:01:50.103
It's Friday at BuzzFeed.

00:01:50.103 --> 00:01:52.100
A ton of free doughnuts right here,

00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:54.631
and I can't eat them because
I'm gluten-free this month.

00:01:54.631 --> 00:01:56.558
Basically, I feel exactly the same.

00:01:56.558 --> 00:01:59.275
- I do not feel more energetic.

00:01:59.275 --> 00:02:01.132
- I wouldn't say I feel
like I have more energy.

00:02:01.132 --> 00:02:02.781
- I actually get up feeling energized

00:02:02.781 --> 00:02:04.870
and ready to get my day going.

00:02:04.870 --> 00:02:07.634
In one week, I've lost about
six and a half pounds already.

00:02:10.284 --> 00:02:12.853
- I'm here to turn things around

00:02:12.853 --> 00:02:15.152
and gonna try some
gluten-free pizza tonight.

00:02:15.152 --> 00:02:16.220
(gasps)

00:02:16.220 --> 00:02:19.029
It's like pizza made on
a too-thick tortilla,

00:02:19.029 --> 00:02:20.492
and they're sweet for some reason.

00:02:20.492 --> 00:02:22.698
It's not a substitute for normal pizza.

00:02:22.698 --> 00:02:23.812
- Better than I thought.

00:02:23.812 --> 00:02:25.345
- I have a feeling that is going to be

00:02:25.345 --> 00:02:27.551
the standard review for gluten-free food.

00:02:27.551 --> 00:02:29.873
- It kinda tastes like pizza minus bread.

00:02:29.873 --> 00:02:31.800
I can't taste the crust at all.

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:33.866
So, I can tell that my body's no longer

00:02:33.866 --> 00:02:36.211
used to eating gluten, but I don't know

00:02:36.211 --> 00:02:38.394
if I'm losing a lot of weight

00:02:38.394 --> 00:02:40.809
or feeling amazingly better.

00:02:40.809 --> 00:02:42.388
- I haven't seen my energy level change.

00:02:42.388 --> 00:02:44.524
I've seen my anger and
frustration level change.

00:02:44.524 --> 00:02:45.455
- Wow!

00:02:46.605 --> 00:02:47.533
What an amazing snack.

00:02:47.533 --> 00:02:48.578
- It's been pretty fantastic.

00:02:48.578 --> 00:02:51.151
I've just found myself walking a lot more,

00:02:51.151 --> 00:02:52.591
not feeling like I need to take a nap

00:02:52.591 --> 00:02:53.543
in the middle of the day.

00:02:53.543 --> 00:02:55.516
So, I'm at my friend's engagement,

00:02:55.516 --> 00:02:57.025
still doing gluten-free, so you can see

00:02:57.025 --> 00:02:58.813
my entire plate is pretty much empty

00:02:58.813 --> 00:03:00.230
besides lentils and rice.

00:03:00.230 --> 00:03:01.460
It's one of those things that I feel like

00:03:01.460 --> 00:03:03.643
I could continue doing
even after this is over.

00:03:06.333 --> 00:03:09.299
- My goal was to just help my girlfriend

00:03:09.299 --> 00:03:11.203
get used to celiac disease,

00:03:11.203 --> 00:03:13.664
and she hasn't had gluten in
maybe three or four months,

00:03:13.664 --> 00:03:16.520
which is huge for her, so
that worked out really well.

00:03:16.520 --> 00:03:18.099
- Nutritionists are really good

00:03:18.099 --> 00:03:20.560
at making gluten-free diets sound fun

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:22.255
when they're actually awful.

00:03:22.255 --> 00:03:23.857
It was too big of an inconvenience.

00:03:23.857 --> 00:03:25.413
- I don't think I really
feel any different at all.

00:03:25.413 --> 00:03:26.992
There's gluten in weird things

00:03:26.992 --> 00:03:28.153
that you wouldn't expect.

00:03:28.153 --> 00:03:29.639
I realized sort of halfway through

00:03:29.639 --> 00:03:31.496
that my face lotion had gluten in it.

00:03:31.496 --> 00:03:33.655
- Now I've found that I
don't really feel bogged down

00:03:33.655 --> 00:03:35.606
by the stuff I've eaten
from the previous day.

00:03:35.606 --> 00:03:36.813
Even just the breakfast I'm having,

00:03:36.813 --> 00:03:38.067
it's a lot lighter.

00:03:38.067 --> 00:03:40.110
I just feel like I've actually got

00:03:40.110 --> 00:03:41.225
energy to get through the day.

00:03:41.225 --> 00:03:42.659
- [Voiceover] You lost five pounds.

00:03:42.659 --> 00:03:44.021
- I lost five pounds, all right.

00:03:44.021 --> 00:03:45.567
- I lost five pounds?

00:03:46.478 --> 00:03:47.708
I don't have a lot of body fat.

00:03:47.708 --> 00:03:50.170
I'm not sure if I can
afford to lose five pounds.

00:03:50.170 --> 00:03:51.725
- [Voiceover] Three pounds of body fat.

00:03:51.725 --> 00:03:53.560
- Three pounds of body fat?

00:03:53.560 --> 00:03:55.034
Oh (bleeped).

00:03:55.034 --> 00:03:55.826
That's cool.

00:03:55.826 --> 00:03:58.636
- I cannot wait to eat gluten again.

00:03:58.636 --> 00:04:00.075
Internet, do you know this?

00:04:00.075 --> 00:04:01.376
Do you know how good pizza is?

00:04:01.376 --> 00:04:02.248
It's so good.

00:04:03.228 --> 00:04:04.598
It is so good.

00:04:04.598 --> 00:04:06.131
- It was worth it just for this plate

00:04:06.131 --> 00:04:07.779
of a cupcake and a pizza.

00:04:07.779 --> 00:04:09.312
This is everything I could've asked for,

00:04:09.312 --> 00:04:10.775
and it just made it that much better

00:04:10.775 --> 00:04:12.302
after not having it for a month.

